# Build output. Covers target/ at any depth, including per-crate directories.
#
# Note: a bare `debug` pattern used to live here. It matched any file or
# directory of that name anywhere in the tree, which silently hid source
# modules named `debug`. target/ already covers target/debug, so it was
# redundant as well as harmful. Do not add it back.
target/

# Backup files generated by rustfmt
**/*.rs.bk

# MSVC Windows builds of rustc generate these, which store debugging information
*.pdb

# Generated by cargo mutants
# Contains mutation testing data
**/mutants.out*/

# Cargo.lock is committed deliberately. Recall ships a binary, so the lockfile
# is what makes a build reproducible. Do not add it here.

# macOS
.DS_Store

# Editors. Prefer a global gitignore for these; kept here so a stray editor
# directory cannot end up in a pull request.
.idea/
.vscode/

# Credentials. SECURITY.md treats a secret reaching the repository as an
# incident. This is the last line of defence, not the first.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key

# Recall's own local session archive (see README > Local Archive).
# Ignored by default; commit it deliberately if session history should be part
# of the project's history.
.recall/
